  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sufentanil</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>N01AH03</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Hahn J et al. 2019</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>critically ill patients supported with extracorporeal membrane oxygenation therapy</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>sufentanil</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>accepted with caveats</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_sufentanil/Sufentanil_Hahn2019_final\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>ΘCL</td><td>37.8</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>ΘV1</td><td>229</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>ΘV2</td><td>1640</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr><tr><td>ΘQ</td><td>41</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>ΘTemp</td><td>0.207</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr></table><h4>About sufentanil</h4><p>Sufentanil is a strong opioid used to treat pain, especially as an anesthetic adjunct and for postoperative pain relief. It remains in use, with an authorised product in the European Union, though it carries a boxed warning and is mainly used in controlled hospital settings such as anesthesia.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417915\">Wikidata Q417915</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Sufentanil\">Sufentanil</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Hahn J et al. (2019). Population pharmacokinetics of intravenous sufentanil in critically ill patients supported with extracorporeal membrane oxygenation therapy. <i>Critical care (London, England) 23(1):248</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-019-2508-4\">10.1186/s13054-019-2508-4</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31288863\">31288863</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Hahn_2019: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"),
